          "title": "Prove measurable and integrable total actual cost",
          "text": "The C2 gradient is measurable, as are the stopped q/N and finite center maps. Therefore the natural count T is measurable. Cast the finite natural sum to the reals. Its constant part is integrable under the full probability law; each first- and second-layer count has L1 integrability supplied by the actual-law parent, so finite addition proves L1 integrability of the actual program count.",
          "formula": "T\\in L^1(\\mu),\\qquad \\mu(\\Omega)=1.",
